# Runtime state. PIDs, the stop flag and the loop scripts are per-machine and
# must never be committed - a stale PID from another host is worse than none,
# and a committed loop script is worse still: compozit.ps1 rewrites it on every
# start, so a server that pulls one gets a permanently dirty working tree and a
# `git pull --ff-only` that aborts mid-release.
#
# This rule only bites on files git is not already tracking. Three loop scripts
# were committed here before it existed and stayed tracked despite it - they now
# live in `examples/`, which is the reference copy of what the generator emits.
# Nothing reads them; nothing here should ever be tracked again.
run/
